'''Archer the Cat''' is a [[:Category:Rare Cats|Rare Cat]] that can be obtained from the [[Cat Capsule#Rare Capsule|Rare Capsule]] during the [[Fate/Stay Night: Heaven's Feel Collaboration Event/Gacha Drop|Fate/Stay Night: Heaven's Feel]] collaboration gacha event. He was added in [[Version 8.2 Update|Version 8.2]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 458
|rarity = RR
|name1 = Archer the Cat
|name2 = Heroic Spirit Archer Cat
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Heroic Spirit Archer Cat''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Archer the Cat, or at least his Evolved Form, is, in short, a worse version of [[Rugby Cat (Rare Cat)|Quarterback Cat]], both being [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance attackers]] with immunity to [[Wave Attack]]s. The former has more health and a slightly lower cooldown, though the latter has nearly twice the DPS, more range, higher pierce, and most importantly, [[Area Attack]]. His lack of Area Attack along with his poor Long Distance coverage means that, ironically, his Normal Form deals better with melee [[:Category:Wave Attack Enemies|Wave enemies]] than his Evolved Form. On top of being outdone by a lukewarm unit, [[Talents|Talented]] [[Kung Fu Cat (Special Cat)|Dancer Cat]] and [[Ancient Egg: N106 (Rare Cat)|Mushroom Cat]] offer more as Wave-immune attackers for Level 4 stages than Archer the Cat ever could. He does, however, has the ability to be obtained far before any of the other aforementioned units. His DPS and [[Single Attack]] are still big issues, so other Long Distance options such as [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]], [[Nymph Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Medalist Cat]] and [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Polevaulter Cat]] have more priority outside of stages with Waves.

